-- title:
--   Over All Outcomes Pasted Sub Expansion Le Dnoteq
-- statement:
--   **Pasted mass exceeds expansion mass by at most the distinctness term.** For the given field-model parameters, strategy, family, and natural number $k$, write $M_p$ and $M_e$ for the pasted and expansion masses. Then
--
--   $$
--   M_p-M_e\le\frac{k^2}{q}.
--   $$
--
--   The quotient is taken in the error type. This estimate measures the loss introduced when passing from the pasted family to the expansion family and is combined with the reverse mass inequality in both over-all-outcomes routes.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.overAllOutcomes_pasted_sub_expansion_le_dnoteq`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
